===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|-|+}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The study of [[handwriting]], especially as a means of [[analyze|analyzing]] a person's [[character]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author=Lee Naftali; Joel Naftali|title=You're Certifiable: The Alternative Career Guide to More Than 700 Certificate Programs, Trade Schools, and Job Opportunities|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=PiMLYH_gY84C&pg=PA155&dq=%22graphology%22%7C%22graphologies%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=TWStU6ivAoOIkwXA1YFg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22graphology%22%7C%22graphologies%22&f=false|page=155
|passage='''Graphology''', or handwriting analysis, is the study and interpretation of handwriting as an indicator of personality. Professional graphologists offer four primary services: '''graphology''' classes to hobbyists, personality profiles to help individuals increase their self-knowledge and potential for change, personnel screening and consultation for employers, and questioned document examination, or forensic '''graphology''', to identify forged handwriting and documents for legal purposes.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2003|author=Michael Hau|title=The Cult of Health and Beauty in Germany: A Social History, 1890-1930|page=50|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=yhd5KbRbJSkC&pg=PT60&dq=%22graphology%22%7C%22graphologies%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=TWStU6ivAoOIkwXA1YFg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22graphology%22%7C%22graphologies%22&f=false|passage=The philosopher Ludwig Klages saw '''graphology''' as a means to penetrate the deceptive self-presentation of his contemporaries and unveil their true character.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Bethan Benwell; Elizabeth Stokoe|title=Discourse and Identity|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=KYO-lOmWLAkC&pg=PA263&dq=%22graphology%22%7C%22graphologies%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=TWStU6ivAoOIkwXA1YFg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22graphology%22%7C%22graphologies%22&f=false|page=263
|passage='''Graphology''' and graphological deviation are likely to be very significant in a mode that lacks non-textual social cues, such as paralanguage, prosody and gesture.}}
# A system of [[handwriting]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1930|author=Frances E. O'Brien|title=Individualism in Child Art|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=lvc8AAAAYAAJ&q=%22graphologies%22&dq=%22graphologies%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=Z3WtU6vrJsOWkQWYqYDAAg&ved=0CPIBEOgBMCc|page=unnumbered
|passage="Talented" children fall into one of two classes: those with an imitative ability who readily absorb the preconceived '''graphologies''' they see about them in pictures, magazines and books, and those{{...}}.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1984|author=David Shapiro|title=Jasper Johns: Drawings 1954-1984|page=29|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=flUkAQAAMAAJ&q=%22graphologies%22&dq=%22graphologies%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=Z3WtU6vrJsOWkQWYqYDAAg&ved=0COkBEOgBMCU|passage=This 1960 work, like the black works of Rauschenberg and the '''graphologies''' of Cy Twombly, is our most patient analysis of multiplicity.}}

